    "pageInfo": "101321",
    "abstractText": "<h4>Introduction</h4>Bladder MRI-guided online adaptive radiotherapy (MRIgART) has enabled a reduction in planning target volume (PTV) margins, reducing normal tissue irradiation. Yet, further margin reduction is limited due to workflow duration and intra-fractional bladder variation. This study reports the feasibility of a 5 mm isotropic PTV in whole bladder MRIgART, 55 Gy in 20 fractions daily, and 36 Gy in 6 fractions weekly, with a personalised approach to margin expansion.<h4>Methods</h4>Patients voided their bladders prior to treatment. Following setup, a daily MRI (MR<sub>DAILY</sub>) was acquired, and an adaptive workflow was performed. An MRI was acquired during delivery to coincide with treatment completion (MR<sub>POST</sub>). Time from MR<sub>DAILY</sub> to MR<sub>POST</sub> was recorded. Offline, target coverage of the clinical target volume (CTV) was visually monitored by comparing MR<sub>DAILY</sub> and MR<sub>POST</sub> images. Images were reviewed by the radiation oncologist (RO) if the CTV was outside of the PTV on the MR<sub>POST</sub>. Under RO discretion, margins were personalised to the minimum margin that would have encompassed the CTV and applied online for subsequent fractions. In retrospective analysis, MR<sub>POST</sub> CTVs were recontoured, and the adaptive plan recalculated. CTV coverage was deemed acceptable if V95% ≥ 95%. If this objective was not met, the gross tumour volume (GTV) was delineated and the dose reported; coverage was deemed acceptable if GTV V95% ≥ 95%.<h4>Results</h4>A total of 138 fractions from ten patients were analysed. Median (interquartile range) workflow time was 25.6 (20.8-30.7) minutes. PTV margins were personalised for 31 fractions in three patients. 119 MR<sub>POST</sub> images were available for analysis. CTV coverage was achieved in 94% (112/119) of fractions. Where the CTV mandatory objectives were missed (6%; 7/119 fractions), GTV coverage was acceptable in 6 of the 7 fractions.<h4>Conclusion</h4>Whole bladder MRIgART with 5 mm isotropic PTV margins with a personalised approach to margin expansion is feasible in achieving acceptable CTV coverage.",
